#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:10
msgid ""
"Built on the shared ``BaseTileScheduler`` skeleton in ``tilelang.language."
"tile_schedule``; see that module's docstring for how ``@meta_class`` "
"inlining and the ``T.alloc_var`` state protocol work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:14
msgid ""
"Next to the raw state accessors, a scheduler hands out the tile scalars a "
"kernel slices with: ``tile()``, plus ``batch()`` / ``group()`` on the "
"variants.  Each call binds its values, assumes their range contract, and "
"returns the bound variables::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:19
msgid ""
"scheduler.init(block_idx)\n"
"while scheduler.valid():\n"
"    m_idx, n_idx, actual_m, actual_n = scheduler.tile()\n"
"    ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:24
msgid ""
"Those assumptions are what lets the pre-schedule passes prove per-tile GM "
"regions and L1/L0 extents in bounds."
msgstr ""

