msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:94
msgid ""
"State lives in single-element ``T.alloc_var`` buffers -- read with ``sched."
"m_idx[0]`` and (inside methods) write with ``self.x[0] = ...``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:106
msgid ""
"Bind the current tile's M/N offsets and extents, and assume their ranges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:108
msgid ""
"Returns ``(m_idx, n_idx, actual_m, actual_n)``: the tile's element offsets "
"along M/N and the in-bounds extents of its M/N tail.  ``actual_m`` / "
"``actual_n`` follow ``get_actual_m`` / ``get_actual_n``, and every tile "
"``_step`` hands out is a grid tile with a non-empty remainder, so the "
"emitted facts hold for every iteration of the ``while sched.valid()`` loop "
"they dominate.  Call it once at the top of that loop body and slice with the "
"returned values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:120
msgid ""
"Decode a linear ``block_idx`` into ``(m_block, n_block)`` (Normal grid)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:144
#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:154
