msgid "Bases: :py:obj:`AscendBaseTileScheduler`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:147
msgid ""
"Single flat M x N grid, GROUP_M swizzle + N-first snake; the last ``< "
"group_m`` M-rows fall back to row-major. This is the plain (non-grouped, non-"
"batched) GEMM scheduler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:157
msgid ""
"Standard batched matmul: the Normal grid replicated ``num_groups`` (= batch) "
"times. ``get_batch_idx()`` exposes the batch of the current block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:160
msgid ""
"Extra parameter ``num_groups`` (= batch count) beyond the base scheduler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:168
msgid "Bind the current batch index and assume its range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:170
msgid ""
"Returns the same bound variable the fact is stated over; use it (instead of "
"the raw ``get_batch_idx()`` read) to slice per-batch GM regions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:180
msgid ""
"MoE m-grouped \"contiguous\" layout. ``grouped_layout`` is the prefix-sum-of-"
"rows array (length ``num_groups``); group ``g``'s valid rows are "
"``[align(psum[g-1], alignment), psum[g])`` in the global M space (group 0 "
"starts at 0). ``get_group_idx()`` exposes the current group for per-group B/"
"SF offsets. A/D must allocate all aligned rows, and physical M must be a "
"multiple of alignment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:186
msgid ""
"Extra parameters beyond the base: ``grouped_layout`` (GM ``int32`` prefix-"
"sum buffer), ``num_groups``, ``alignment`` (group-start row alignment, "
"default 256)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:198
msgid "Bind the current group index and assume its range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:200
msgid ""
"``valid`` gates the loop body on ``group_idx < num_groups``; the m cursor is "
"``last_psum_m // block_m + <group-local tile>``, so it stays non-negative "
"and every full tile fits the padded row space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:211
msgid ""
"MoE k-grouped. All groups share one M x N grid but differ in K length; "
"``grouped_layout[i]`` is the cumulative end-K of group ``i``. "
"``get_group_idx()``, ``get_k_idx_base()`` / ``get_sf_idx_base()`` give the "
"group and its A/B and SF K offsets; ``get_shape_k()`` is the current group's "
"K length."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:216
msgid ""
"Extra parameters beyond the base: ``grouped_layout`` (GM ``int32`` prefix-"
"sum buffer), ``num_groups``, ``shape_k`` (physical K allocation, including "
"trailing padding; only the K-range contract uses it), ``alignment`` (group-"
"start K alignment, default 256)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:236
msgid "Bind the current group's K window and assume its ranges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:238
msgid ""
"Returns ``(group_idx, k_base, group_k, sf_base)``: the group index, the "
"group's K origin, its K length, and the origin of its packed scale-factor "
"rows.  A valid tile belongs to a non-empty group, so the K span ``[k_base, "
"k_base + group_k)`` stays inside the total K and its SF rows stay inside the "
"packed SF buffer: a group starts on an ``alignment`` boundary, which is a "
"multiple of the SF divisor."
msgstr ""
